WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:03.830
What do you mean, "hand over O-Tae"...?

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:06.420
I mean what I said.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:10.830
I want Tae Hanazono to join my band,
RAISE A SUILEN, officially.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.750
Hang on, you can't just drop
something like that on us...

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:15.830
Are you really a producer?

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:20.130
Yes. I'm the boss when it comes to
RAISE A SUILEN, or RAS for short.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:23.660
I do everything from writing music to
choreographing performances.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:25.620
Th-thanks...

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.670
So, what did you think of our
self-sponsored show tonight?

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:30.420
It was amazing!

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:31.580
Really...

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.040
Left you speechless, huh?

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:34.920
CHU2!

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:44.880
Sorry! We've got an after party to run to.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:46.540
See you around.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:48.460
Let's go, Hanazono.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:49.410
Okay.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.380
Thanks for coming tonight!

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:29.460
I got the official okay from Chisato-san.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:30.540
What?

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:34.960
For PasuPare to be guests at our show.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:38.170
Ah! Really? That's great!

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:40.170
Start with that next time, okay?

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:42.220
You scared me for a second...

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:43.790
Okay...

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.330
You guys seem weird today.

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:49.080
Um...

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:54.630
After the show, that girl, CHU2 came up
to us and... asked us to hand you over.

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:55.540
What?

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:58.920
She said she wanted to officially 
scout you for RAS...

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:01.540
Scout me? Why would...

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:06.500
CHU2 did mention that she 
wanted to meet you guys.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:09.000
She asked when all five 
of us would be together.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:13.460
I'll tell her no.

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:16.420
Are you sure?

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:17.700
Well...

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:19.040
How about today?

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:19.750
What?

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:22.330
We're getting together after school, right?

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:24.090
Ask her to come see us then.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:26.040
You really think we should meet?

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:28.130
Well, ignoring her won't make this go away,

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:31.330
and we can't prepare for the show
the way things are now, right?

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:36.040
Amazing!

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.080
A secret studio!

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:40.750
Wow, look at all these vintage treasures!

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:42.420
This! And this!

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:45.580
Awesome! Where'd you get it?!

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:47.790
Uh... It was all my grandpa's...

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:50.250
Your grandpa?! Excellent!

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.420
CHU2-sama, your official greeting.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:54.750
I-I know!

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:59.420
Thank you for taking the 
time to see us today.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:02.920
Does everyone here like sweets?

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:06.040
I'll just cut to the chase, here.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:09.850
I'd like for Tae Hanazono 
to quit Poppin' Party.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:10.830
But why?

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:16.080
Isn't it obvious? You don't have the energy
to play in two bands at once.

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:20.210
But you already announced that
last weekend was O-Tae's last show.

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:23.540
Yes! Her last show as a support guitarist.

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:27.830
Now Hanazono will be starting fresh
as an official member.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:30.500
It's important to note that difference.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:34.080
Don't you think... that's a little selfish?

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.710
Shouldn't O-Tae get a say?

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:40.210
Yeah. But I didn't really see a point
in talking to Hanazono alone.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:41.960
Can I have one of these?

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:42.880
Sure...

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:47.130
Poppin' Party is a band you all
formed as friends, right?

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:48.890
R-right.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:53.890
Don't you think that friendship
might be holding Hanazono back?

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:57.710
Why O-Tae?

00:04:57.710 --> 00:04:58.710
Why?

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:00.880
You went to our last show, didn't you?

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:04.630
Perfect sound, perfect 
songs, perfect performance!

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:07.040
Our place is center stage, in the spotlight!

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.880
It's in the name- RAISE A SUILEN!

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:10.170
We're unstoppable!

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:11.460
Yes! Unstoppable!

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:14.750
In this girl band era, 
we're rising to the top!

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:16.830
No- we're changing the world!

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:19.460
We'll forge our own girl band era!

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:21.670
And Hanazono's got the soul to help us do it!

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:26.670
RAISE A SUILEN was created as
an expression of the music CHU2-sama creates.

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:29.830
All of the members were chosen via audition.

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:33.330
We haven't been together very long yet,
but everyone's been amazing so far.

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:37.920
I'll be sad to see you go.

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:40.880
As will the fans, of course. And Layer.

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:45.580
It's like your seven years 
apart never happened.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:47.670
The groove you two have is real.

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:54.330
Hana-san, didn't you have fun
playing in a band with us?

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:56.670
Well, I...

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:01.660
You can give me your answer
after your self-sponsored show.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:06.250
I look forward to hearing from you,
dear friends of Hanazono.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:14.390
CHU2-sama can come across a little harsh,
but I can vouch for her taste.

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:18.920
She pulled me up out of 
the darkness, after all.

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:20.920
Pareo!

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:22.630
Coming, Mistress!

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:25.380
Well, it was lovely seeing you all!

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:28.710
CHU2-sama! Wait for me!

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:31.460
I'm sorry...

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:32.880
O-Tae...

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:34.460
Don't apologize.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.620
I'm the one who said she should come here.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.420
I... I'm going to-

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:41.540
You don't have to decide right now.

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:43.670
Saaya...

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:46.830
I think you should really 
give it some thought.

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:47.800
What?

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:51.960
What I really wanted was to slap
that annoying face of hers...

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:55.210
but the band really acknowledges your talent,

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:58.880
they've got big goals,
and the skills to back them up...

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:00.710
I didn't know what to say.

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:05.290
I'll practice at home today...

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:08.750
O-Tae!

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:18.830
Sorry... all I did was push things off.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:20.040
It's okay.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:22.920
When we saw them play the other day,

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:27.420
part of me felt like maybe 
O-Tae should join them...

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:32.130
That bassist-vocalist, Layer...

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:36.100
I actually went to the same music school
as her a long time ago.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:38.600
Rei Wakana.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:42.330
I never really spoke to her
since we studied different things,

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:44.580
but her singing voice was pretty famous...

00:07:46.670 --> 00:07:50.670
Those two... they must have
known each other back then.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:59.290
CHU2, what were you thinking?

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:00.960
What?

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:03.850
You never told me you 
were scouting Hana-chan.

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:05.630
Are you against it?

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:09.080
Don't you want to keep playing with Hanazono?

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:22.580
Sis...

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:25.790
Sorry, A-chan! Could you shut my alarm off?

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:29.040
Thanks!

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:31.960
Ugh, you were already up?

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:33.380
Be back later.

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:36.210
See you...

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:46.580
Yamabuki Bakery

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:48.460
PoPiPa
PiPo
Party
Poppin' Party First Self-Sponsored Live!

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:53.880
Why do I always feel like this...

00:08:57.170 --> 00:08:58.790
Ah, Kasumi-chan.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:00.790
Hello!

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:03.170
Why don't you come inside, dear?

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:04.210
Arisa!

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:06.880
Maybe she's still asleep.

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:09.540
Their sound could soon make them
the new leaders of the
girl band generation.

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:08.920
It's all right!

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:38.140
Twinkle, twinkle, little star,

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:43.080
how I wonder what you...

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:49.520
Hydrangea Fair

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:49.520
I put together some temporary choreography

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:52.000
based on the set list you gave me,

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:53.920
but what about the new song?

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:56.210
Um...

00:09:56.210 --> 00:09:59.540
Oh! Sorry, I was spacing 
out! You were saying?

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:02.130
Did something happen after last time?

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:06.380
You always guess when something's up, huh...

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:08.130
I-I'm sorry!

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:09.540
It's okay.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.210
Hey, Lock?

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:14.250
PoPiPa... we're still PoPiPa, right?

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:15.210
What?

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:18.960
Y-yeah! PoPiPa are still PoPiPa!

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:24.290
You shine up on stage, always have fun,
and every time I watch you perform, I just think...

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:28.920
Wow! Being in a band must be so much fun!
And I love that feeling, and-!

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:32.150
I love you guys when you're 
not on stage too, though!

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:34.960
Thanks.

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:36.960
I love PoPiPa too!

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:03.040
O-Tae...

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:06.130
Hey.

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:16.920
Aren't you cold?

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:17.830
Nah.

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:21.040
I just stopped by Galaxy.

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:24.410
I thought it'd be good to actually stand up on stage when picking colors

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:26.460
for the lighting and stuff.

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:27.710
Yeah.

00:11:27.710 --> 00:11:32.500
Oh, and I ran into Maya-san when I
went to take fliers to the music shop.

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:37.130
She asked me for a list of all the equipment
on stage, so I've gotta send that later.

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:38.180
Yeah.

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:41.630
Oh yeah, I also went by the warehouse.

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:42.540
Yeah.

00:11:43.710 --> 00:11:45.290
I wasn't sure...

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:49.880
The thought of quitting PoPiPa
had never even entered my mind.

00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:53.380
But you guys told me to 
really think about it...

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:59.280
We all want what's best for you, O-Tae.

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:01.860
We care about you a lot.

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:03.240
You do?

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:04.500
Yeah.

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:11.500
The RAS show was really amazing.

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:14.210
You guys were so cool.

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:18.920
I'd never seen you perform like that before,
and that shook me up a little bit.

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:25.170
I thought... this could 
really be O-Tae's future.

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:29.680
But PoPiPa are still PoPiPa.

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:34.250
O-Tae and Rimi-rin, Saaya, Arisa, and me.

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:38.330
We can still see each other
during lunch and after school.

00:12:38.330 --> 00:12:40.880
You'll always be able to play with us.

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:42.710
You're part of PoPiPa!

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:45.840
Let's play some guitar, O-Tae!

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:48.420
I didn't bring an amp.

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:12.920
Such a weirdo.

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:42.800
Club
Show

00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:54.140
Hanasakigawa Girls' Academy High School Cultural Festival
Blossom
Festival

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:12.250
O-Tae?

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:13.920
a faraway sky

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:15.170
the farther we're separated

00:15:15.170 --> 00:15:16.680
"future"
we can reach for

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:22.420
heart-shaking

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:28.750
intertwined

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:35.790
Let's go.

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:45.170
PoPiPa
Kasumi: Arisa, Rimi-rin, Saaya,
can you come to the warehouse? 
PoPiPa
Tae: I want you to hear something.

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:46.630
I'll be back later!

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:48.630
Huh?

00:15:53.090 --> 00:15:54.800
Sorry I'm late!

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:57.420
It's okay, have a seat.

00:15:57.420 --> 00:15:58.420
Okay!

00:15:58.420 --> 00:15:59.830
Saaya, how about here?

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:12.460
I put all my feelings into this.

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:14.670
Hope you like it.

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:33.290
I... I love PoPiPa.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:35.380
Kasumi...

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:36.960
Rimi...

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:38.710
Arisa...

00:18:39.040 --> 00:18:40.290
Saaya...

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:46.460
Arisa?

00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:50.330
One more time.

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:51.250
What?

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:52.960
Sing it again.

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:54.000
Okay.

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:22.080
You know, I don't hate PoPiPa,
and being in a band is pretty fun.

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:28.000
Who knows what'll happen in the future,
but having a goal together, the five of us...

00:19:28.880 --> 00:19:33.710
even aiming to perform at the Budokan
someday doesn't seem so bad...

00:19:36.750 --> 00:19:42.250
But I didn't really know
how you felt about all this, O-Tae.

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:47.420
I thought maybe you'd be okay
playing with another band...

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:51.460
Now I understand.

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:54.340
But, you know...

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:57.580
you didn't have to write a song about it.

00:19:57.580 --> 00:19:59.580
It's so like you, though...

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:01.670
Arisa.

00:20:02.170 --> 00:20:04.920
I didn't know how to say it either...

00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:12.130
I didn't want you to leave us,
but I thought that was selfish of me.

00:20:12.880 --> 00:20:15.830
I... I just can't.

00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:20.920
I thought I'd finally learned 
how to say how I feel...

00:20:22.710 --> 00:20:25.330
O-Tae, don't go...

00:20:26.540 --> 00:20:27.750
I won't.

00:20:28.250 --> 00:20:30.210
I'm not leaving, Saaya.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:36.830
Thanks, Rimi-rin.

00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:37.540
Huh?

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:42.460
I was so afraid you'd tell us
you were quitting PoPiPa today,

00:20:42.460 --> 00:20:46.560
so Rimi-rin came and picked me up
so we could come together.

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:47.710
Rimi...

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:52.500
I know how much you love PoPiPa, O-Tae-chan.

00:20:53.210 --> 00:20:58.250
Thanks for always caring 
about this band so much.

00:20:58.250 --> 00:21:04.830
I want to keep working even harder
to support you, and the rest of us, too...

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:09.330
I feel so lucky to have PoPiPa.

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:12.540
I...

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:15.250
I...

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:18.540
O-Tae.

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:19.880
O-Tae-chan.

00:21:20.540 --> 00:21:22.170
O-Tae...

00:21:23.420 --> 00:21:26.250
I'm so happy!

00:21:26.250 --> 00:21:27.790
Get off, Kasumi!

00:21:27.790 --> 00:21:28.830
No!

00:21:28.830 --> 00:21:30.130
Kasumi!

00:21:30.130 --> 00:21:31.710
Arisa!

00:21:30.130 --> 00:21:37.060
Star Tears

00:21:31.710 --> 00:21:32.920
Rimi!

00:21:32.920 --> 00:21:33.170
I'm so glad!
Rimi!

00:21:33.170 --> 00:21:35.250
I'm so glad!
Saaya!

00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:36.170
I'm so glad!

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:41.040
Arisa!

00:21:41.580 --> 00:21:43.210
It's getting late...

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.140
Next episode: Returns
